==Specials==
====Schwarze Flamme====
{{FrameDataCargo-COTW
|name=Schwarze Flamme
|moveId=kain_236A,kain_236C,kain_236AC
|input=236P
|description3= * Kain's iconic fireball returns as a zoning and combo tool. Has a feint that looks similar to the fireball and still backsteps.
* All versions cause Kain to backstep, which can get you out of sticky situations, but can lead Kain to making combos harder or cornering himself in neutral if used improperly.
* A version fires horizontally, C version fires diagonally upwards. REV version covers both angles.
* All versions are useful in corner combos, but the REV version is particularly useful for both midscreen and corner routes.

}}

====Schwarzer Panzer====
{{FrameDataCargo-COTW
|name=Schwarzer Panzer
|moveId=kain_236B,kain_236D,kain_236BD
|input=236K
|description3= * Fairly reasonable combo tool. All versions are identically unsafe on block.
* B version starts traveling fastest, D version does the most damage and has a few starting hits, and the REV version can be cancelled into 28BD to make it + on block.
* All versions have a brake, but only the B version properly brakes at point blank. None of the brakes work after a connect.
* The REV version is most used as a combo extender off juggles or heavies, while the B and D version are used as combo enders and work on lights (though the D version can fall out at range). 
*  The D version is Kain's best meterless guard cancel option without down charge.
|display=300x150px
}}

====Schwarze Lanze====
{{FrameDataCargo-COTW
|name=Schwarze Lanze
|moveId=kain_28B,kain_28D,kain_28BD
|input=[2]8K
|description3= * Kain's flashkick is a versatile tool, usable as a combo starter, extender, ender, anti-air, pressure tool, and reversal.
* Since this move has a quicker-to-execute input than a DP motion, Kain has an advantage in reacting to certain moves with invincibility. He makes up for this with needing down charge to do reversals, which limits his movement in neutral and ability to block overheads if he wants to use this move.
* The B version is a decently fast reversal, the D version is a solid anti-air with a brake. The REV version is a combo extender, and can be braked to become + on block.
* If possible, the D version (and its respective brake) is usually Kain's best Guard Cancel after JD/HD, though could prove difficult to execute.
* Even if the fireball connects on a grounded opponent, Kain is at major disadvantage, so only use it in situations where the first hit can connect.
* The fireball can hit OTG. This usually happens when the first hit connects on an extended limb or at its max range, keeping Kain safe on hit.
}}

====Schwarzes Rondo====
{{FrameDataCargo-COTW
|name=Schwarzes Rondo
|moveId=kain_214A/C,kain_214AC
|input=214P
|description2= * Kain's new mine special compliments both Kain's pressure and space control, making it a versatile move.
* The B and D versions create a mine at 2 different distances, and the REV version creates both mines.
* All versions will automatically detonate with a delay, or can be input again to manually detonate.
* The REV version will detonate both mines at the same time automatically, but will stagger and combo if done manually.
* All versions can compliment Kain's Schwarze Flamme, putting another thing on the screen for the opponent to worry about.
* Most combos Kain scores, along with his throw, can lead to him placing a Schwarzes Rondo on top of the opponent. This gives Kain looping pressure if he desires, which usually leaves him majorly plus if the opponent blocks it successfully.
}}

====Schwarzes Rondo (Detonate)====
{{FrameDataCargo-COTW
|name=Schwarzes Rondo (Detonate)
|moveId=kain_214A/C_detonate,kain_214AC_detonate
|input=(After 214P) 214P
